# A real macOS .app: an icon, generated plists, and the resource files the
# program reads at run time. Everything except the two Bundle keys is an
# ordinary build file - bundling is a packaging step on top of a normal
# executable, not a different kind of project.

# The .app is a macOS thing, so say so instead of quietly building a bare
# executable everywhere else.
Assert.Platform macos

Assembly        Sundial
SourceDirectory src

# Metadata. On Windows these fill the version resource; here they are what
# RiftBuild writes into Contents/Info.plist and Contents/version.plist -
# CFBundleName, CFBundleShortVersionString, CFBundleIdentifier
# (com.<CompanyName>.<Assembly>) and the rest.
# The (define) parameter additionally injects SUNDIAL_VERSION_STRING into
# every source file, so the program prints the same version the plist claims.
Version(define) 1.2.0
TitleName       Sundial
Description     Tells the time the old way
CompanyName     Artisan Softworks
Copyright       Copyright (C) 2026 Artisan Softworks

# No extension: RiftBuild picks Sundial.png here (and would pick Sundial.ico
# on Windows). sips and iconutil turn the png into a six-size Sundial.icns
# that lands in Contents/Resources, and the generated Info.plist already
# points CFBundleIconFile at it.
Icon Sundial

# The flag that wraps the freshly linked executable in Build/Sundial.app.
# Build/Sundial itself stays where it is - the bundle gets a copy.
Bundle

# ...and makes it a *terminal* app: the executable moves to Sundial-bin and
# CFBundleExecutable becomes a tiny shell script, so double-clicking the app
# in Finder opens Terminal and runs the program there. Drop this line for a
# GUI app.
Bundle.IsTerminal

# Anything the generated Info.plist does not already say goes in as
# Info.plist.<key>. Values are written as <string> unless they are whole
# numbers (<integer>) or written as "(a b c)", which becomes an <array>.
# NSHumanReadableCopyright is the one Finder's Get Info panel shows, and the
# generated plist has no such key - $Copyright pastes the value set above
# rather than saying it twice.
Info.plist.NSHumanReadableCopyright  $Copyright
Info.plist.LSMinimumSystemVersion    11.0
Info.plist.LSApplicationCategoryType public.app-category.utilities
Info.plist.NSHighResolutionCapable   true

# Bundling happens before PostBuild, so this is where the program's own data
# files go. Contents/Resources already exists at this point - Sundial.icns is
# sitting in it.
PostBuild
{
    Copy assets/* Build/Sundial.app/Contents/Resources
}

# Uncomment to launch the finished app at the end of every build. (.Run would
# run the bare executable in Build/ instead of the bundle.)
# PostBuild.Cmd open Build/Sundial.app
